## Part 1: Regulatory Authority - CAS2 Table 2.2 Note 7

### Official Regulatory Text

**Source:** C/AS2: Acceptable Solution for Buildings with Sleeping (non-institutional) or Crowd Activities, Table 2.2, Page 40, Note 7

**Exact Text:**
> "In buildings with an Occupancy WB, where:
> - the occupant load is 10 to 99, and
> - storage is greater than 3 m in height,
>
> a Type 3 fire alarm system is required as an alternative to the Type 9 automatic sprinkler system shown in the table."

### Regulatory Interpretation

**Risk Group:** WB (Working - Business/Storage)

**Conditions (ALL must be met):**
1. Risk group is WB
2. Occupant load is in range 10-99 (inclusive on both ends)
3. Storage height is greater than 3 meters (>3.0m, not ≥3.0m)

**Action:** Add Type 3 system to fire safety systems

**System Type 3 Definition:** "Automatic fire alarm system activated by heat detectors"

**Note Behavior:**
- This is an **ADDITION** note - it ADDS Type 3 to the system requirements
- It does NOT remove any systems
- Type 3 is added ONLY if not already present (deduplication required)

